WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.535
-Another thing
that seems to, uh...

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.537
seems to be splitting
the way Democrats think,

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.138
not just
the idea of electability

00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:07.406
but also the idea
of impeachment --

00:00:07.406 --> 00:00:09.075
is this a fool's errand?

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.743
I think you have many
in the party who think

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:12.445
this is a man who's done
plenty of things

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:16.248
that are why we have
impeachment as an option

00:00:16.248 --> 00:00:17.650
and others who are saying,

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.587
"No, we need to focus on the
ballot box as a way of removal."

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.054
What do you think?

00:00:22.054 --> 00:00:24.024
-I think this is another one
of those things where Democrats

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:25.692
are sort of
outthinking themselves,

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.527
like in the same way
with the electability thing.

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:29.562
Like, you may really want
to beat Donald Trump.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.564
You can't personally work out

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:34.200
who's the most electable
candidate to win the primary.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.736
In the same way, impeachment --

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:38.437
you sort of
can't really game out

00:00:38.437 --> 00:00:41.173
what the political impact
of impeachment is going to be.

00:00:41.173 --> 00:00:43.709
That's not the kind of process
impeachment is.

00:00:43.709 --> 00:00:45.478
If a president commits crimes,

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.212
commits high crimes
and misdemeanors,

00:00:47.212 --> 00:00:50.049
the way the Congress is supposed
to hold him accountable

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:51.750
is by opening
an impeachment inquiry,

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:53.719
doing an investigation,
and then voting

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:56.055
on whether or not they think
that it rises to that level.

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:58.624
Whether or not that hurts the
President, helps the President,

00:00:58.624 --> 00:01:01.427
hurts the Democrats,
helps the Democrats,

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:03.229
A, is unknowable,

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.231
and, B,
should be beside the point.

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:07.066
And if you're doing it
for the right reasons,

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:09.569
I think you are more likely
to persuade the country

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:11.270
that you've done it
for the right reasons

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:14.206
rather than you having tried to
think everybody around a corner,

00:01:14.206 --> 00:01:16.075
in terms of how
this is supposed to work out.

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:19.178
I just think just be --
Approach these things simply.

00:01:19.178 --> 00:01:20.446
Pick the best candidate

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:22.081
who you think would make
the best president.

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:23.583
Approach impeachment

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.718
in terms of the Constitutional
imperative here.

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:26.986
Who cares who it's good for?

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.521
-It does strike me, as well,

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:32.124
whether he is impeached or not,
he'll act like he was impeached.

00:01:32.124 --> 00:01:33.926
-Yes.
Yes, yes.

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:35.728
-And, you know, he's gonna --
he's not gonna --

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:37.397
if he doesn't get impeached,
say, "You know what?

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:39.164
That was a real fair shake
I got from the Democrats.

00:01:39.164 --> 00:01:41.267
I tip my hat."
-Yeah, exactly!

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:44.136
-"I may have been wrong
about those bozos."

00:01:44.136 --> 00:01:46.672
-It's true.
They're gonna run campaign ads.

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:48.408
He's gonna give speeches
talking about them

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:50.810
being socialists
who want to impeach him.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:51.944
There's nothing you can do

00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:53.379
to make him
not call you a socialist.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:54.680
-Right.
-Just do what you think

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.181
is right.
He's gonna call you names.

00:01:56.181 --> 00:01:58.551
If you're really lucky, he'll
give you a diminutive Nickname.

00:01:58.551 --> 00:01:59.952
-Yeah.
-Congratulations.

00:01:59.952 --> 00:02:01.253
-Yeah, that'd be a winner.

00:02:01.253 --> 00:02:02.988
-There's no way that you can
get around that stuff.

00:02:02.988 --> 00:02:04.857
And he will --
And the Republicans

00:02:04.857 --> 00:02:06.926
will all campaign
as if the Democrats

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:09.028
are just "impeachment-mad
socialists,"

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:11.030
so just
do what you think is right.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.198
Don't worry about
what people say about you.

00:02:13.198 --> 00:02:16.402
-We both talked about
Trump's adventures in Europe,

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:17.670
and that was just --

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.806
in general, I just found a peace
with him being there

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:23.376
just because it shifted by five
hours when things could happen.

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:24.977
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:26.645
You know, at like 9:00,
if I was at dinner,

00:02:26.645 --> 00:02:27.680
I had a thought of, like,

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:28.814
"If I haven't
heard anything now,

00:02:28.814 --> 00:02:30.249
he's probably asleep,"
you know?

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:31.351
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:32.751
But you --
-You were so good, though.

00:02:32.751 --> 00:02:35.654
When you described him as, like,
every American tourist thing

00:02:35.654 --> 00:02:38.757
that anybody has ever done wrong
anywhere in the world,

00:02:38.757 --> 00:02:40.359
he's doing them all at once.
-Yeah.

00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:41.761
-Like,
that's exactly what he was.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.129
When you described him that way,

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:44.930
I was like,
"That's what he's doing!"

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.700
He's embodying all of
the worst stereotypes

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.236
that everybody in the world
has about dumb Americans,

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:52.338
and he's living them large!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.340
Like, with their leaders.
It was just...

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:55.708
-Yeah. Well, you can tell
they look at him,

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:56.809
and they're not saying,

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:58.111
"Oh, I've met a guy
like this before."

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.679
They're like, "I've met
a guy like this before,

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.514
but it was 100 different guys."
-Yes.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:02.915
[ Laughter ]
-Like, this --

00:03:02.915 --> 00:03:05.284
He's like a Voltron
of all of it.

00:03:05.284 --> 00:03:07.387
-Yeah.
-You had a wonderful --

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:08.821
I had not seen this photo
that you called out

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.089
on your show last night,
which is,

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:12.124
here's the Trump family
in a picture.

00:03:12.124 --> 00:03:14.293
And I will say, they all look
lovely, beautiful gowns.

00:03:14.293 --> 00:03:15.427
-The Trump adult children.
-Trump adult children.

00:03:15.427 --> 00:03:16.496
-Why are they there?

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:17.964
They don't work
for the government.

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:20.099
-Who pointed this out to you?
Did you find this on your own?

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:23.503
-So, I was reading
the Irish press because,

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:24.870
as you talked about
on your show, as well,

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:26.672
Trump goes over to Ireland
and is like,

00:03:26.672 --> 00:03:29.408
"Yeah, about your border wall
with Northern Ireland..."

00:03:29.408 --> 00:03:31.244
It's like,
"Dude, there's no border wall

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:32.345
with Northern Ireland."

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:34.280
And that's
a really sensitive subject!

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.449
please don't go there.
Ugh!

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:38.317
So, I was looking at
the Irish press

00:03:38.317 --> 00:03:41.420
to see how they covered
that disaster by the President,

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:43.689
and what I found
was they were like,

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:45.725
"Hey, look at this picture
of the Trump adult children.

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:47.626
Isn't that lovely, how they're
posing for that photo?"

00:03:47.626 --> 00:03:49.461
-That's great but we're gonna
zoom in on something over here.

00:03:49.461 --> 00:03:50.929
Right there.
"No photos."

00:03:50.929 --> 00:03:53.499
-"No photographs."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:55.735
-They literally --
They literally are like,

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.636
"Let's take a picture,"
and they're like,

00:03:57.636 --> 00:03:59.705
"Well, not over there, 'cause
it says 'no photographs.'"

00:03:59.705 --> 00:04:01.974
And they're like,
"No, let's do it there."

00:04:01.974 --> 00:04:03.409
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:06.378
-The President's whole family
poses in front of

00:04:06.378 --> 00:04:07.813
the "No Photos" picture.

00:04:07.813 --> 00:04:09.014
Yep, that's pretty much
our lives now.

00:04:09.014 --> 00:04:11.383
-That's their style.
That is their style.

00:04:11.383 --> 00:04:12.851
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:04:12.851 --> 00:04:15.821
-I want to be serious
here for a second,

00:04:15.821 --> 00:04:19.158
because you've done
a really good job of covering

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:22.362
a very scary situation right now
with all the abortion laws

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:23.729
that are being passed
at the state level.

00:04:23.729 --> 00:04:25.298
-Yeah.
-And, obviously, there was

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:27.132
a lot of talk
about what Alabama did,

00:04:27.132 --> 00:04:29.601
but there's also a lot happening
in Missouri right now

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:31.403
where there are basically
efforts being made

00:04:31.403 --> 00:04:35.708
to close the last
abortion provider in the state.

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:37.676
-Yeah.
-Can you talk a little bit

00:04:37.676 --> 00:04:39.378
about, like, what actually
is happening there

00:04:39.378 --> 00:04:41.480
and how punitive it is,

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:42.781
these laws
that they're talking about?

00:04:42.781 --> 00:04:44.550
-The thing that's different
about what's happening

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:47.586
in Missouri right now
is that they are the closest

00:04:47.586 --> 00:04:50.323
any state has ever been
to completely ending

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:52.891
legal abortion access
in the entire state.

00:04:52.891 --> 00:04:55.627
No state has been able
to do that since Roe vs. Wade

00:04:55.627 --> 00:04:57.863
was passed
by the Supreme Court in 1973.

00:04:57.863 --> 00:04:59.832
But for the first time,
Missouri's state government,

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:01.367
the Republican-controlled
state government,

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:05.271
is trying to shut down the last
abortion provider in the state.

00:05:05.271 --> 00:05:08.307
So they're trying to take
the last clinic's license away.

00:05:08.307 --> 00:05:11.177
And as they are doing that, the
state government has come in,

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:13.345
and they have told the doctors
at that clinic

00:05:13.345 --> 00:05:16.115
that while they're still open
and while women are still able

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:18.250
to get abortions there,
the doctors at that clinic

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:23.556
must now start giving medically
unnecessary pelvic examinations,

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:28.060
like vaginal examinations,
to women, specifically --

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:31.096
basically, as the cost of them
asking for an abortion.

00:05:31.096 --> 00:05:32.564
So, it's medically unnecessary.

00:05:32.564 --> 00:05:35.134
The doctors don't want to do it.
There's no reason to do it.

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:37.970
The women who are getting
abortions do not want this done,

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:40.072
and the state government
has come in and mandated

00:05:40.072 --> 00:05:44.343
that they get this extra
internal exam

00:05:44.343 --> 00:05:46.478
while they're trying
to shut down that last clinic.

00:05:46.478 --> 00:05:49.515
And so, we've been reporting
on that for the past week or so.

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:51.717
The state government in Missouri
got very mad at us

00:05:51.717 --> 00:05:53.919
about reporting on it,
but it's freaking true.

00:05:53.919 --> 00:05:55.988
And we went to the clinic
and talked to the staff there

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:58.724
about how they are being forced
to do this to their patients now

00:05:58.724 --> 00:05:59.759
on orders of the state.

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:01.794
And it's just --

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:04.297
I think it's upsetting, I think,
to a lot of people,

00:06:04.297 --> 00:06:06.899
both the state of abortion
rights around the country

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:08.167
and what's going on in Missouri,

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:09.635
but the fact that they're
doing that to these women

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:10.937
on order
of that state government

00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:13.238
is just sort of
horror-movie disturbing.

00:06:13.238 --> 00:06:15.174
-Well, we certainly appreciate
you guys actually getting

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:16.475
on the ground there
and going and talking

00:06:16.475 --> 00:06:18.444
to those people 'cause that
is incredibly informative

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:19.778
and necessary
at times like these.

00:06:19.778 --> 00:06:21.346
[ Cheers and applause ]
Last thing I want to ask.

00:06:21.346 --> 00:06:23.982
-Yeah.
-You are, in the middle

00:06:23.982 --> 00:06:25.618
of all this --
moderating debates,

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:27.919
hosting your own show --
you are writing a book, as well.

00:06:27.919 --> 00:06:30.923
Just to like relax and unplug,
you're writing a book.

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:33.926
Is it a fun --
It's a fun romantic-comedy romp?

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:34.993
Is that a safe way
to describe it?

00:06:34.993 --> 00:06:38.197
-Yeah, it's a romantic
little ditty

00:06:38.197 --> 00:06:40.566
about the geopolitics
of the oil and gas industry.

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:43.736
[ Laughter ]
-Rachel!

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:46.405
Rachel, no!

00:06:46.405 --> 00:06:49.207
-No, I do that.
You know, I do some vaping.

00:06:49.207 --> 00:06:51.443
It's, like, pretty much, like,
It's my kicking downtime.

00:06:51.443 --> 00:06:52.945
-"Blowout."
It's called "Blowout."

00:06:52.945 --> 00:06:54.614
-It's called "Blowout."
It comes out October 1st.

00:06:54.614 --> 00:06:55.681
Yeah, I'll come back
and talk to you about it.

00:06:55.681 --> 00:06:57.116
-Okay, great.
I look forward to it.

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:58.918
It's always great to see you.
That's Rachel Maddow, everybody.

